JIT Core

JIT Core is an embeddable dynamic recompilation core for ARM-family guest code.

The current code targets AArch32 ARM, Thumb, and AArch64 instruction behavior. It provides guest CPU state, instruction decoding and execution paths, trace construction, memory access hooks, exception callbacks, cycle accounting, and helpers for preserving translated execution state.

JIT Core is meant to be embedded by a host program. The host supplies memory access, fallback handling, timing control, and system callbacks. The core keeps CPU behavior separate from the host environment so the same library can be used in different runtimes.

The public project name is JIT Core.
